File / Folder	Purpose
dist/	Contains production-ready HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and assets generated when we run npm run build.
node_modules/	Contains installed dependencies and packages required by the project.
public/	Stores static files such as favicons, public images, and documents that don't need to be imported into JavaScript.
src/	Contains the main application source code, components, pages, and local images.
src/assets/	Stores assets such as local logos, images, and SVG files imported into components.
src/pages/	Typically contains page-level components, such as Login, Dashboard, and Home.
App.jsx	The root application component that organizes the UI and other components.
main.jsx	The entry point that mounts the React application into the DOM.
App.css	CSS styles specifically associated with the app or its components, depending on how you organize your project.
index.css	Typically contains global styles applied across the application.
index.html	The HTML template containing the root element where React mounts the application.
package.json	Contains project metadata, scripts, and dependency information.
vite.config.js	Contains Vite configuration, such as plugins, development server settings, and build options.

